# READ-FIELD-CLOSURE (T7), a local named Structure's free name in a callable merge's node: model runs its local S,
# whose `v: cnt` reads cnt, a free name of S that model forwards as its hidden input; model returns S\v.  The root's
# own binding of cnt is 9 when it calls w, and the caller's binding comes first (docs #dynamic); the copy of the unit
# made at the merge, holding 7, is only the lexical fallback.  9.  (Registered red until 2026-10-08 with 7 expected: a
# wrong oracle, withdrawn by Codex's audit of K03-READ-FIELD-CLOSURE-20261008-31.)  Exit 7; 81 otherwise.
int: cnt 7
fn: model (int: y) int
    S:
        int: v 0
        v: cnt
    S
    return: S\v
fn: wrap (int: k) fn: () int
    return: merge(y: k; model)
@: w wrap(5)
cnt: 9
int: result w()
int: ok 7
if: result != 9
    ok: 81
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
